<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/9th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Qarqar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">853 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Qarqar was fought in 853 BCE near the Orontes river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> between the Assyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-iii">Shalmaneser III</a> and a coalition of twelve kings led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadadezer-of-damascus">Hadadezer of Damascus</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urhilina">Irhuleni</a> of Hamath and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahab">Ahab of Israel</a>. Shalmaneser claimed victory on the Kurkh Monolith, but his advance into Syria was halted for years. The inscription is the earliest non-biblical reference to a king of Israel.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-qarqar.jpg" alt="Battle of Qarqar" width="173" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yuber · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karkar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
